     <h2>3. Recording of data on our website</h2>
     <p><strong>Cookies</strong></p>
     <p>In some instances, our website and its pages use so-called cookies. Cookies do not cause any damage to your computer and do not contain viruses. The purpose of cookies is to make our website more user friendly, effective and more secure. Cookies are small text files that are placed on your computer and stored by your browser.</p>
+    <p>We use a session cookie only to remember your reading list. It is not used for advertising or to track you across other websites.</p>
+
+    <h2 id="account">4. Accounts</h2>
+    <p>To create an account we ask for a username and a password, and nothing else: no email address, real name, or phone number. Your username does not need to identify you. These details are sent only to our account service and are used to create your account and sign you in.</p>
+    <p>The sign-in and sign-up pages load no third-party analytics or advertising scripts, and are never stored in your browser's cache.</p>
+
+    <h2 id="analytics">5. Analytics</h2>
+    <p>On article and section pages we load an analytics script that records which links and buttons are clicked. For each click it sends the element type (link or button), its visible text, and the time of the click. It does not record what you type into forms, and it does not run on the sign-in or sign-up pages.</p>
+
+    <h2 id="third-parties">6. Third parties and your browser</h2>
+    <p>Our fonts are hosted on our own servers, so reading the site does not send your IP address to a font provider.</p>
+    <p>When our pages request resources from other websites, your browser sends at most our domain name as the referrer, never the article you are reading. Browser features such as your camera, microphone, location, and motion sensors are disabled on every page for us and for any embedded content.</p>
 </LegalLayout>
